{
  peppy_schema: "launcher/v1",
  description: [
    "A botshare base in a simulation: Waldo, unless a launch word selects another simulation, and one simulated botshare base named alpha, botshare.ai's OpenAMRobot 2.0 base on two driven wheels. It opens no device, so it launches on a machine with no botshare hardware.",
    "The simulation is the stack, and the robot is a copy, alpha, a simulated botshare base that base_motion's goals drive, its ids minted under its name: alpha_init_inst, alpha_backbone_inst. `stack remove` takes a copy off and `stack join` adds one, the simulation running throughout, and `--join OPTION:NAME` names another copy at launch.",
    "`peppy stack launch botshare_simulation`: Waldo and one botshare base.",
    "`peppy stack launch botshare_simulation --with mujoco`: the same base in MuJoCo.",
    "`peppy stack launch botshare_simulation --with isaac_sim`: the same base in Isaac Sim.",
    "`peppy stack launch botshare_simulation --with robot_control`: the base driven over MCP.",
    "`peppy stack launch botshare_simulation --with robot_control,alpha.cameras_sim`: driven over MCP, its depth camera served.",
    "`peppy stack launch botshare_simulation --with robot_control,alpha.lidar_sim,alpha.room_mapper`: driven over MCP, mapping the rooms it drives in with its lidar, saving the maps by name and localized in the loaded one.",
    "`peppy stack launch botshare_simulation --with alpha.drive_controls`: alpha driven by hand from Waldo's page, with its stick, the arrow keys or a gamepad.",
    "`peppy stack launch botshare_simulation --with xr_commander`: alpha driven by hand from the stack's headset, in any simulation.",
    "`peppy stack launch botshare_simulation --with robot_control,alpha.cameras_sim,alpha.base_navigator`: driven over MCP, its navigator driving it around what its depth camera sees.",
    "`peppy stack launch botshare_simulation --with robot_control,alpha.lidar_sim,alpha.room_mapper,alpha.base_navigator`: driven over MCP, its navigator driving it around what its lidar sees, and to poses in the room mapper's loaded map.",
    "`peppy stack join botshare_sim:bravo`: another botshare base beside alpha.",
    "The robot axis offers the botshare base alone, and every simulation stands as many as the machines can run, each joined copy bringing its own. A copy named with `--join` is composed as a join, as `stack join` is, and a join cannot turn rendering on: the simulation renders when the copy this launcher lists selects its rig, as the fifth command above does, and `--with cameras_sim` on a join is refused on a launch without one.",
    "`--with robot_control` serves the robots' MCP endpoint, http://127.0.0.1:8900/robot_control/v1/mcp, where every robot is listed and a model drives the base through base_motion, and through base_navigation where its navigator runs, reads its odometry, stops it, sees through its depth camera and, on a base that maps, maps the rooms, saves and loads the maps and localizes the base in them, and the framework's, http://127.0.0.1:8903/framework_controls/v1/mcp, where a client halts the stack and adds no robot.",
    "`--with alpha.drive_controls` gives alpha Waldo's drive controls as its commander, which lead its base on drive_link; Waldo's page lists every base that selects them and drives the one chosen. `--with xr_commander` runs the stack's headset, which leads every base that runs no commander of its own and no navigator, one at a time, chosen on the headset's page. `--with alpha.base_navigator` gives alpha its navigator, which leads its base for base_navigation's goals. A base has one leader: the drive controls under Waldo alone, the headset, or its navigator.",
    "simulation_mcp stands the base beside the arm robots in one simulation: `peppy stack launch simulation_mcp --join botshare_sim:india`.",
  ],

  components: [
    {
      name: "simulation",
      cardinality: "one",
      provides: ["simulation_inst"],
      options: {
        mujoco: "simulation/fragments/mujoco.json5",
        isaac_sim: "simulation/fragments/isaac_sim.json5",
        waldo: "simulation/fragments/waldo.json5",
      },
    },
    // The robots' MCP endpoint, selected with `--with robot_control`, and
    // the framework's endpoint beside it, whose fleet tools halt the stack.
    // Every robot is listed on the robots' endpoint with its moves.
    {
      name: "robot_control",
      cardinality: "zero_or_one",
      options: {
        robot_control: {
          fragments: ["mcp/fragments/framework_controls.json5", "mcp/fragments/robot_control.json5"],
        },
      },
    },
    // The stack's teleoperation headset, selected with `--with
    // xr_commander`: a base running no commander of its own and no navigator
    // pairs into it, and the headset drives the one chosen on its page.
    {
      name: "teleop",
      cardinality: "zero_or_one",
      options: {
        xr_commander: "teleop/fragments/xr_commander.json5",
      },
    },
    // The simulated botshare base, an option of the same name in every
    // launcher that offers it. Every simulation stands any number of them.
    {
      name: "robot",
      cardinality: "zero_or_more",
      options: {
        botshare_sim: {
          fragments: ["botshare/fragments/botshare_sim.json5"],
          adjustments: [
            // Listed on the MCP endpoint: who it is, its guide, where it
            // carries its sensors and where its frames stand, what its base is
            // and where its odometry places it, and the moves a model drives
            // it by with the stop that ends them.
            { target: "robot_control_inst",
              add_links: { identity: ["init_inst"], guide: ["init_inst"], sensor_mounts: ["init_inst"],
                           transform_lookup: ["transforms_inst"], base_state: ["backbone_inst"],
                           base_motion: ["backbone_inst"], robot_stop: ["backbone_inst"] } },
            // Listed on the MCP endpoint with profile and geometry.
            { target: "robot_control_inst", when: { camera_rig: "cameras_sim" },
              add_links: { depth_camera: ["base_camera"], camera_profile: ["base_camera"], camera_geometry: ["base_camera"] } },
            // The navigator's tools, listed beside the moves.
            { target: "robot_control_inst", when: { navigator: "base_navigator" },
              add_links: { navigator: ["navigator_inst"] } },
            // Listed on the MCP endpoint with its maps and its place in the
            // loaded one, while it maps with its lidar.
            { target: "robot_control_inst", when: { mapper: "room_mapper" },
              add_links: { room_map: ["mapper_inst"] } },
            // Rendering, while this robot films.
            { target: "simulation_inst", when: { camera_rig: "cameras_sim" },
              set_arguments: { cameras_enabled: true } },
            // The stack's headset leads a base with no commander of its own
            // and no navigator: the backbone pairs into it (the robot's
            // fragment), and a squeeze stops the base's moves in flight
            // through its robot_stop.
            { target: "headset_inst", when: { teleop: "xr_commander", robot_commander: "none", navigator: "none" },
              add_links: { robot_stop: ["backbone_inst"] } },
            // The stack's headset shows the base's camera while it leads it.
            { target: "headset_inst", when: { teleop: "xr_commander", robot_commander: "none", navigator: "none", camera_rig: "cameras_sim" },
              add_links: { rgbd_cameras: ["base_camera"] } },
          ],
        },
      },
    },
  ],

  // Component deployments: the entry names the component and its option,
  // and the robot entry lists the copy the launch starts, set up as its
  // fragment deploys it; `--join OPTION:NAME` names another.
  deployments: [
    { simulation: "waldo" },
    { robot: "botshare_sim", instances: [{ instance_id: "alpha" }] },
  ],

  adjustments: [
    // The server reads the simulation's clock, as every instance a robot
    // copy runs does; each simulated robot's fragment binds its own.
    { target: "robot_control_inst", set_framework: { clock: "simulation" } },
    // The framework's endpoint serves its fleet target alone: this file
    // offers an MCP client no robot to add, so its stack target stays
    // vacant, and every robot joins from the command line.
    { target: "framework_controls_inst",
      set_daemon_scopes: { stack: { vacant: "this launcher offers MCP clients no robot to add: robots join from the command line" } } },
    // The stack's headset reads the simulation's clock like every instance
    // a robot copy runs does, and Waldo's headset panel shows it: the link
    // that opens its page in the headset.
    { target: "headset_inst", set_framework: { clock: "simulation" } },
    { target: "simulation_inst", when: { simulation: "waldo", teleop: "xr_commander" },
      add_links: { headsets: ["headset_inst"] } },
    // The headset holds the cameras of the robot it drives at their own
    // rate through Waldo's sensor streams, which render them at 1 Hz while
    // no client holds them.
    { target: "headset_inst", when: { simulation: "waldo", teleop: "xr_commander" },
      set_links: { sensor_streams: "simulation_inst" } },
  ],
}
